# Which physical board the flashing tools are allowed to write to.
#
# PLACEHOLDER ONLY. Copy to tools/bench.local.ps1 and fill in. That file is
# gitignored, because a unique device ID is a device identifier in the same
# class as a MAC address and does not belong in a repository.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. More than one Zephyr board lives on this bench, they expose
# identical CDC-ACM shells, and at least one of them enumerates with the same
# USB VID:PID as this one. Over DFU there is NO signature check - dfu-util
# writes whatever it is given to whatever address it is given - so a
# mis-targeted install would overwrite another board's bootloader. The OTA path
# is protected by the per-project signing key and by asking the board its name;
# the DFU path has neither, so it gets this.
#
# The value is the USB serial reported by `dfu-util -l`, which on an STM32 is
# the chip's unique device ID. Run tools/install_mcuboot.ps1 with no bench file
# and it will print the serial it found and refuse to write, which is the
# intended way to discover it.

$PMC_DFU_SERIAL = ''
